      "message": "\u003e Do you know why there are no header file changes required to get access to USEC_PER_MSEC?\n\nPassing `-E` to the compiler to run the preprocessor shows that it\u0027s getting transitively included from `include/zephyr/kernel.h` through `zephyr/kernel_includes.h`. I didn\u0027t dig through the chain that is including `zephyr/kernel.h`; it looks like it\u0027s from some generated syscall code.\n\n\u003e Also, is there a way to find out if any source files no longer need access to the header containing MSEC (src/platform/ec/include/timer.h, generally)?\n\nI don\u0027t think you can do it without building. But we can use this [new check](https://crrev.com/c/6221870) to progressively eliminate calls to functions in `ec/include/timer.h` and then add another check that blocks includes of `timer.h`.",
